# Keep the Docker build context small and free of large/secret/local data.
# `**/target/` catches every Cargo build dir (root, crates/*, fuzz/…), which
# otherwise dominate the context (GBs of artifacts).
**/target/
target/
exav-db/
corpus/
fuzz/
tmp/
docs/
packaging/
.git/
.github/
.claude/
.env
.env*.local
*.cache
*.exavdb
yara-x/
# `**/`, as with target above: a bare `node_modules/` matches only one at the
# root of the context, and both of this repo's are nested — `www/` (282 MB) and
# `crates/exav-unpack-wasm/` (60 MB). They appear the first time anyone runs the
# docs site or the JS suite, and from then on every image build ships 342 MB it
# does not use, slowly enough to exhaust the open-file limit and fail outright.
**/node_modules/
# Generated the same way and just as unused by the image: the built docs site
# and the wasm-pack output.
www/dist/
**/pkg/
